  "verbalization": "Quisqualic acid appears to interact with PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1 through a series of intermediate targets, suggesting a complex network of molecular interactions. The evidence indicates that Quisqualic acid targets 5-oxoprolinase and G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1, both of which are subsequently targeted by other molecules, ultimately leading to the activation of CDC2L1. This suggests that Quisqualic acid may influence cellular processes through these intermediates, potentially affecting mitotic regulation or cell cycle progression. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CDC2L1 implies a possible role in cell cycle control or response to stress, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of CDC2L1 in cellular functions, and the involvement of Quisqualic acid in this process may be a key regulatory step.",
